 Community feedback</div>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://www.producthunt.com/products/skybridge\" target=\"_blank\">Skybridge</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Full-stack open source React framework for building MCP Apps. Handles infrastructure and dev loop so developers can focus on features. Write once, run in Claude, ChatGPT, VSCode, and any MCP client.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <span class=\"meta-tag\">AI development framework</span>\n                        <span class=\"meta-source\">Product Hunt • Jun 23, 2026</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://www.producthunt.com/products/jebi\" target=\"_blank\">jebi</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        A supercharged terminal for Mac with built-in local AI that provides intelligent suggestions after each command. No API key, subscription, or cloud required.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <span class=\"meta-tag\">AI terminal</span>\n                        <span class=\"meta-source\">Product Hunt • Jun 23, 2026</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://www.producthunt.com/products/conduit\" target=\"_blank\">Conduit</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Local MCP gateway that fixes tool-list bloat in AI agents by routing tools through one local gateway, reducing token overhead by 97% with 3 meta-tools for on-demand searching.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <span class=\"meta-tag\">AI agent tooling</span>\n                        <span class=\"meta-source\">Product Hunt • Jun 22, 2026</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n            </section>\n\n            <!-- Whitelist Updates Section -->\n            <section class=\"whitelist-updates\">\n                <h2 class=\"section-header\">Whitelist Updates</h2>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://code.claude.com/docs/en/whats-new\" target=\"_blank\">Claude Code</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"update-title\">Week 24 Releases (v2.1.166-v2.1.176)</div>\n                    <div class=\"update-description\">\n                        New /cd command to move sessions to new working directories, nested sub-agents that can spawn their own agents, safe mode for isolating broken states, and improved OpenAI integration. Added two new cybersecurity features.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"update-date\">Jun 8-12, 2026</div>\n                    <div class=\"community-quote\">\n                        \"Comprehensive guides covering 25+ Claude Code features with examples published mid-June 2026\"\n                        <div class=\"quote-source\">— Releasebot (Positive)</div>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://cursor.com/changelog\" target=\"_blank\">Cursor</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"update-title\">Cursor 3.8 - /automate skill and new triggers</div>\n                    <div class=\"update-description\">\n                        Introducing /automate skill for creating automations in local agent sessions. Added new GitHub triggers, Slack emoji triggers, and cloud agents now support computer use. Bugbot: 3x faster, 22% cheaper, finds 10% more bugs.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"update-date\">Jun 22, 2026</div>\n                    <div class=\"community-quote\">\n                        \"Reports of Cursor dominating AI IDE rankings in 2025-2026 with Composer, Agent mode, and multi-model support\"\n                        <div class=\"quote-source\">— Chinese Developer Reports (Positive)</div>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://github.blog/changelog/2026-06-03-github-copilot-in-visual-studio-code-may-releases/\" target=\"_blank\">GitHub Copilot</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"update-title\">May 2026 releases (v1.120-v1.123)</div>\n                    <div class=\"update-description\">\n                        Agents window available in VS Code Stable as preview, expanded BYOK to air-gapped environments, new remote agents over SSH/Dev Tunnels, Agent Host Protocol (AHP), session preferences persist, and session sync.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"update-date\">Jun 3, 2026</div>\n                    <div class=\"community-quote\">\n                        \"Starting April 24, 2026, GitHub will begin using your Copilot data for improving Copilot\"\n                        <div class=\"quote-source\">— Reddit (Neutral)</div>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://docs.devin.ai/release-notes/overview\" target=\"_blank\">Devin</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"update-title\">MCP Marketplace Expansion - 48+ new engineering MCPs</div>\n                    <div class=\"update-description\">\n                        Added 48+ new engineering MCPs including Miro, Mixpanel, Honeycomb, Postman, monday.com, Klaviyo, and others. Devin Desktop was renamed from Windsurf on June 2, 2026.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"update-date\">Jun 19, 2026</div>\n                    <div class=\"community-quote\">\n                        \"Discussion about programmers shifting focus from Prompt Engineering to MCP in 2026\"\n                        <div class=\"quote-source\">— Reddit (Neutral)</div>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/changelog\" target=\"_blank\">Codex CLI</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"update-title\">Codex CLI 0.142.0 - Usage reset credits and plugin improvements</div>\n                    <div class=\"update-description\">\n                        Adds /usage command for reset credits, /plugins organizes remote plugins into sections, configurable rollout token budgets, multi-agent delegation controls, and scheduled UTC time reminders.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"update-date\">Jun 22, 2026</div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://geminicli.com/docs/changelogs/\" target=\"_blank\">Gemini CLI</a>\n                        <span class=\"closed-badge\">SHUTDOWN</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"update-title\">Gemini CLI Shutdown - June 18, 2026</div>\n                    <div class=\"update-description\">\n                        Google is shutting down Gemini CLI for free, Pro, and Ultra users on June 18, 2026. Users need to migrate before this date.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"update-date\">Jun 18, 2026</div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://windsurf.com/changelog/vscode\" target=\"_blank\">Windsurf</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"update-title\">Changelog updates - May 2026</div>\n                    <div class=\"update-description\">\n                        Released v2.2.17 (May 5) and v2.0.44 (May 16) with chat improvements, UI enhancements, command improvements, and enterprise updates. Note: Ownership changes with Cognition acquisition.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"update-date\">May 16, 2026</div>\n                    <div class=\"community-quote\">\n                        \"Windsurf went through ownership changes (Cognition acquisition) and leadership departures to Google, creating uncertainty about product direction\"\n                        <div class=\"quote-source\">— 2026 Review (Neutral)</div>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://aider.chat/HISTORY.html\" target=\"_blank\">Aider</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"update-title\">No major releases in June 2026</div>\n                    <div class=\"update-description\">\n                        Latest stable release is v0.86.2 (February 12, 2026). Last repository push was May 22, 2026. Aider continues as a git-first, open-source alternative to proprietary solutions.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"update-date\">May 22, 2026</div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://github.com/continuedev/continue/releases\" target=\"_blank\">Continue</a>\n                        <span class=\"acquired-badge\">ACQUIRED</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"update-title\">Acquired by Cursor</div>\n                    <div class=\"update-description\">\n                        Continue has been acquired by Cursor. Their mission states that developers should be 'amplified, not automated'. Final 2.0.0 release available for VS Code extension, CLI, and JetBrains plugin.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"update-date\">Jun 1, 2026</div>\n                </div>\n            </section>\n\n            <!-- Technical Insights Section -->\n            <section class=\"technical-insights\">\n                <h2 class=\"section-header\">Technical Insights</h2>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"insight-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=46330726\" target=\"_blank\">LLM Year in Review</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"insight-description\">\n                        Claude Code highlighted as the most impressive innovation of the year, noted as a significant improvement over Cursor as a coding tool.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"insight-meta\">\n                        Hacker News Community • Jun 20, 2025\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"insight-topics\">\n                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">Claude Code</span>\n                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">Cursor</span>\n                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">tool comparison</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"insight-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://magazine.sebastianraschka.com/p/llm-research-papers-2025-list-one\" target=\"_blank\">LLM Research Papers: The 2025 List</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"insight-description\">\n                        A curated list of over 200 research papers from 2025, organized by topics. Comprehensive coverage including DeepSeek R1, multi-agent frameworks, and more.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"insight-meta\">\n                        Sebastian Raschka • Jun 18, 2025\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"insight-topics\">\n                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">LLM research</span>\n                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">DeepSeek R1</span>\n                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">multi-agent</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"insight-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=44257283\" target=\"_blank\">2025 State of AI Code Quality</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"insight-description\">\n                        Discussion exploring issues with LLM responses degrading massively and becoming useless, requiring users to start over. Community concerns about code quality when using AI tools.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"insight-meta\">\n                        Hacker News Community • Jun 18, 2025\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"insight-topics\">\n                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">LLM</span>\n                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">code quality</span>\n                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">AI limitations</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"insight-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=44623953\" target=\"_blank\">Coding with LLMs in summer of 2025</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"insight-description\">\n                        Discussion about how local AI inference has been heavily restricted by limited memory capacity and high prices of consumer graphics cards. Community discussing practical limitations and solutions.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"insight-meta\">\n                        Hacker News Community • Jun 17, 2025\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"insight-topics\">\n                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">LLM</span>\n                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">local inference</span>\n                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">hardware</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"insight-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=44623953\" target=\"_blank\">Context Bloat in AI Coding Tools</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"insight-description\">\n                        Emerging concern about context window management in long coding sessions. Tools like Sipcode addressing 40% agent error reduction through context hygiene.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"insight-meta\">\n                        Community Research • Jun 22, 2026\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"insight-topics\">\n                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">context management</span>\n                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">performance</span>\n                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">tooling</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"insight-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://docs.devin.ai/release-notes/overview\" target=\"_blank\">MCP as the New Prompt Engineering</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"insight-description\">\n                        Discussion about programmers shifting focus from Prompt Engineering to MCP (Model Context Protocol) in 2026 as the primary skill for AI agent development.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"insight-meta\">\n                        Reddit Community • Jun 19, 2026\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"insight-topics\">\n                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">MCP</span>\n                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">skill shift</span>\n                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">agent development</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n            </section>\n        </div>\n    </main>\n\n    <footer>\n        <a href=\"#\">Archive</a>\n        <a href=\"#\">About</a>\n        <a href=\"#\">Methodology</a>\n        <a href=\"#\">GitHub</a>\n        <a href=\"#\">Subscribe</a>\n        <div style=\"margin-top: 8px;\">\n            Generated with Claude Code • © 2026 Agentic Coding Research\n        </div>\n    </footer>\n</body>\n</html>"
